  <!-- Module Settings -->

  <title>Module Settings</title>

  <section id="xiphos-modules-parallel">
    <title>Parallel</title>

    <media style="image" mime="image/png"
	   src="figures/preferences_modules-parallel.png" />
    <p>The <gui>Parallel</gui> tab lets you create sets of Bible books
    that you want to view side by side.</p>
    <media style="image" mime="image/png"
	   src="figures/preferences_modules-misc.png" />
  </section>

  <section id="xiphos-modules-special">
    <title>Special</title>

    <p>The <gui>Special</gui> tab gathers the default modules <app>Biblia Elim</app>
    falls back on for particular kinds of lookups, so you do not have to
    choose a source module every time:</p>

    <list>
	<item>
	<p><gui>Daily Devotional</gui> - the Daily Devotional module used to
	populate the <link xref="xiphos-11-interface#xiphos-devotional">Devotional
	tab</link>.</p>
      </item>
	<item>
	<p><gui>Hebrew Lexicon</gui> - the module
	consulted when you hover over a Strong number, so that
	Hebrew strong codes are shown.</p>
      </item>
	<item>
	<p><gui>Greek Lexicon</gui> - the module
	consulted when you hover over a Strong number, so that
	Greek strong codes are shown.</p>
      </item>


      <item>
	<p><gui>Hebrew Morphology Lexicon</gui> - the module
	consulted when you hover over an Old Testament in Hebrew morphology tag, so that
	Hebrew morphological codes resolve to their meaning even in Bible
	modules that do not carry their own morphology dictionary link.</p>
      </item>
	  <item>
	<p><gui>OT Greek Morphology Lexicon</gui> - the equivalent
	setting for Old Testament morphology tags, resolving Greek
	morphological codes (parts of speech, tense, case, etc.).</p>
      </item>
      <item>
	<p><gui>NT Greek Morphology Lexicon</gui> - the equivalent
	setting for New Testament morphology tags, resolving Greek
	morphological codes (parts of speech, tense, case, etc.).</p>
      </item>
	 <item>
	<p><gui>Default Dictionary</gui> - the dictionary module used when you
	double-click a word anywhere in <app>Biblia Elim</app>, if the <gui>Default
	Dictionary</gui> option is enabled in
	<link xref="xiphos-50-preferences-general-settings"/>.</p>
      </item>
    </list>

    <p>These selectors are populated from whatever suitable dictionary and
    devotional modules you already have installed; install one first from the
    Module Manager if the list is empty. See also
    <link xref="xiphos-33-original-language"/> for setting these up as part of
    original-language study.</p>
  </section>
